# Customer copy (release notes and Help)

Write for the person using the desk, not the diff. Same voice on
`/release-notes` and Help / page help / FAQ.

## Do

- Lead with the benefit, then one concrete what. One idea per bullet.
- Keep it short. Easy to scan. Each point unique.
- Vary the opener in a group. Mix *It's now easier / quicker / clearer*,
  *We've simplified / tidied / shortened / dropped / opened*, *You can now*,
  *Finding X is faster*, *X no longer*. Do not start every line the same way.
- Name the surface the customer sees (Add bet, Home, Fixtures). Link `href`
  to that page when one exists.
- British English, sentence case, commas. Run `customer-copy.test.ts`.

## Do not

- List layout, tokens, component names, or ticket IDs.
- Explain how it was built, or rename things unless the customer will
  notice the new name.
- Repeat the same benefit verb in one group, or stack three Add bet
  bullets that are really one change.
- Leak providers or internals (D8). The LEAK regex in
  `customer-copy.test.ts` is the floor, not the voice.

## Examples

```
Bad:  Early payout is a tinted strip under the Back plate, switch left.
Good: We've tidied Early payout onto a strip under Back, so the extra
      fields only appear when you need them.

Bad:  Cash balance is now Balance. Light wash, not a grey plate.
Good: It's now easier to see if you can fund the bet. Balance sits
      under Back and Lay.
```
